Wake word "Zordon" (voice/models/zordon-wake-v1.npz, SPEC-013, ADR-0038).
The detector uses feature models and code adapted from openWakeWord
(https://github.com/dscripka/openWakeWord, Apache License 2.0), including
Google's speech_embedding model (Apache License 2.0). The classifier was trained
by this project with data under the following licenses:

  Multilingual LibriSpeech, Portuguese and Italian   CC BY 4.0  Pratap et al., Meta AI
                     https://www.openslr.org/94/
  LibriSpeech train-clean-100   CC BY 4.0  Panayotov, Chen, Povey, Khudanpur
                     https://www.openslr.org/12/
  LibriTTS-R (via Piper en_US-libritts_r-medium)  CC BY 4.0  Koizumi et al.
                     https://www.openslr.org/141/
  TTS-Portuguese Corpus (via Piper pt_BR-edresson-low)  CC BY 4.0  Edresson Casanova
                     https://github.com/Edresson/TTS-Portuguese-Corpus
  Piper voices pt_BR faber, cadu, jeff (datasets CC0)
                     https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices

Third-party components are listed in docs/security/supply-chain.md, pinned with
versions in gradle/libs.versions.toml, and enumerated in the CycloneDX SBOM
published with each release (`./gradlew sbom`). Model files are pinned by URL,
SHA-256 and size in voice/models.lock.
